<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Marciano, 33, comes for his yearly preventive visit five weeks after intake and three weeks after the sports medicine consultation. He is in his fourth week of physical therapy and his back pain is easing; the leg pain has stopped. He wears the thumb splint for gripping work and at night and uses the gel. He is walking every day and swimming twice a week and has cut down his portions, and his weight is down by 1.4 kg. His home blood pressure readings over the week after intake averaged 126/78 mmHg. He has been taking naproxen most days after his exercises rather than only when needed. He has no stomach pain, black stools or heartburn. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 33</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Lumbar disc herniation with resolving sciatica; chronic low back pain; thumb-base osteoarthritis; overweight; elevated blood pressure reading at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Naproxen 500 mg, now most days; diclofenac 1% gel on the left thumb</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-2 0</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Written questionnaire completed by the patient in the waiting room and reviewed with him by Dr. Fairweather-Obi. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Very good, apart from his back</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Married with a young daughter; enjoys being home; plenty of work from appearances and business</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol and drugs</td><td>An occasional glass of wine; AUDIT-C 1 at intake; no drugs; never used anabolic steroids</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks daily and swims twice a week; physical therapy twice a week</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Smaller portions than in training camp; more vegetables and fish; fewer second helpings</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven hours; wakes less with back pain than a month ago</td></tr><tr><td>Driving and injury</td><td>Wears a seat belt; does not text while driving</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Smoke alarms working; no firearms in the home</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>One partner; no concerns</td></tr><tr><td>Dental</td><td>Regular dentist; an old chipped front tooth from the ring was repaired years ago</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

