    <td>R03.0</td><td>S — Synthetic finding after the end of heavy training; resolved with weight loss and exercise.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-6">
    <td>History of repetitive head impacts from about thirteen years of Army, amateur and professional boxing, including heavy sparring; no remembered loss of consciousness; normal brain health baseline (no cognitive, mood or behavioral complaints; MoCA 29); traumatic encephalopathy syndrome not suspected</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z87.828</td><td>S — Synthetic risk-factor problem anchored to his documented career and sparring; no concussion or brain injury is documented in the sources read.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

