    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated. At 33, with blood pressure in the elevated range, no diabetes and no tobacco, his 10-year cardiovascular risk is low; the LDL of 137 mg/dL at intake calls for diet and exercise, not a statin. HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening drawn today. [S]<list><item>First hepatitis B vaccine dose today; second in one month.</item><item>Influenza and this season&apos;s COVID-19 vaccine when they arrive in the autumn.</item><item>Results of the screening tests by phone.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Lumbar disc herniation with radiculopathy (M51.16)</content>. Leg pain resolved and the numbness fading in the fourth week of physical therapy. [S]<list><item>Continue physical therapy as planned.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>126/78 mmHg; home average 126/78 mmHg, elevated range without hypertension</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid screening and statin</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Total cholesterol 212, HDL 45, LDL 137, triglycerides 148 mg/dL at intake; low 10-year risk; diet and exercise; repeat in about five years or sooner if risk changes</td></tr><tr><td>Prediabetes and type 2 diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>HbA1c 5.4% and glucose 91 mg/dL at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Begins at 45</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Routine one-time screening for ages 15 to 65</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>One-time screening for all adults</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Triple panel, once for all adults</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 0; PHQ-9 3 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Anxiety screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>GAD-7 4 at intake, minimal</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use</td><td>Up to date</td><td>AUDIT-C 1 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco cessation</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Healthy weight and physical activity</td><td>Completed today</td><td>BMI 28.3; meal plan and exercise prescription from the consultation under way</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap six years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 of 2 (HepB-CpG) today; dose 2 in one month</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>When this season&apos;s vaccine arrives in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Offered with the influenza vaccine in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Declined</td><td>Routine vaccination ends at 26; from 27 to 45 it is a shared decision, and with one long-term partner he chose not to</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), dose 1 of 2, recommended for all adults 19 to 59 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (2025); 2026 ACC/AHA/AACVPR/ABC/ACPM/ADA/AGS/APhA/ASPC/NLA/PCNA Guideline on the Management of Dyslipidemia (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Physical therapy continues. Second hepatitis B dose in one month. Screening results by phone. Eight-week review at the end of September. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 1956-09-29: eight-week review: back pain after six weeks of physical therapy, the thumb splint, the stomach after stopping naproxen, weight and blood pressure. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
